{#-
  The CSS sheet, handed to WeasyPrint through genalog unchanged.

  genalog's own templates build a page out of the content they are given;
  this one does not build anything. `generators/html/sheets/` has already
  produced a whole `<!doctype html>` document -- the same string the browser
  backend loads -- and the only job here is to let genalog's Jinja
  environment and its `Document` wrapper hand it to WeasyPrint.

  That is the point: one markup, two engines. A template that rebuilt the
  page from parts would be a third renderer wearing the second one's name,
  and the two would drift the first time either was edited.
-#}
